    "narrative": "With the league title race tightening, Ghost Ride the WHIP leans into a high-upside offensive construction today. Our strongest play is undoubtedly **Mickey Moniak**, who sits at a 75.98 efficiency score. While facing a formidable arm like Michael King, **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive park factor boost and an ideal platoon alignment that pushes him into the \"Strong\" start tier. Similarly, **Isaac Paredes** (65.76) is a lock in our three-hole, buoyed by a favorable matchup against Seth Lugo (xERA 4.59) and a situational boost for his premium spot in the order. Both players are expected to anchor our production in runs and RBI today, as we look to capitalize on these specific matchup advantages.\n\nIn contrast, we have reached the limit of our \"Marginal\" start threshold with **Moises Ballesteros** (56.00) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (56.11). **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains a steady contributor, but without a confirmed starter, we have to remain cautious regarding potential lineup shuffling. The most difficult decision today involved **Brice Turang** (55.40); while his elite sprint speed makes him a critical asset in our pursuit of stolen bases, his efficiency is suppressed by a difficult matchup against an elite defensive catcher and a sub-optimal matchup against the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill set. We are keeping **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, **Josh Naylor**, **James Wood**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Cole Young** on the bench due to team off-days, forcing us to rely on our active core to maintain our pace in the 5x5 standings.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given that **Moises Ballesteros**, **Trevor Story**, **Isaac Paredes**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino** are still waiting on official lineup confirmation. **Trevor Story** (49.52) is the most precarious start on our roster; his score barely cleared the floor, and his reliance on a specific batting order position makes him the first candidate to be pulled if we receive news that he is dropping further down the lineup. We are monitoring local weather reports closely, as any wind shifts could further erode the marginal gains currently propping up **Moises Ballesteros**. We proceed with these starts to maximize our daily floor, but we are ready to adjust if the confirmed lineups shift our expected output.",
